            <ArticleTitle>Acute thrombosis of drug eluting stent following protamine: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reversal of anticoagulant effect of heparin to treat coronary perforation after bare metal stent implantation is an accepted practice. However this practice may not be safe following drug eluting stent implantation. We report a case of acute stent thrombosis following protamine administration for coronary perforation after drug eluting stent implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
